Cleaner: keep dep as `(state: LocalState) => Promise<SaveResult>` and update the 7 test stubs to `saveLocalState: async () => ({ state: localState })`? But stubs don't have the input... they can echo: `async (state) => ({ state })`. Easy.

But wait — controller tests also assert `saved.value?.history[...]`; echoing works fine.

Also the notice on warning: if saveState returns warning (corrupt-moved-aside), showNotice it. Good for visibility.

Let me also keep behavior when saveLocalState throws: track() shows notice. Good.

Now check: in `readForMerge`, on JSON parse failure I rename to `.corrupt-<ts>` — data preserved, warning returned. controller shows notice. Good.

One more: `Bun.sleep` — is that available in config module context? Yes, used elsewhere? Check style guide — it's Bun runtime. OK.

Let me fix the tail-cleanup logic to be simpler and re-write those parts.

